{"title":"Dr. Lyndon B. Duff","markdown":{"headingText":"Dr. Lyndon B. Duff","containsRefs":false,"markdown":"\n![](images/profile.png){fig-align=\"center\" width=\"35%\"}\n\n### Behavioural Ecology • Social Ecology • Foraging Behaviour\n\nI am a behavioural ecologist interested in the ecological and evolutionary processes that shape social organization, cooperation, dispersal, and reproductive behaviour in bees.\n\nMy research combines long-term field studies, social-network approaches, and statistical modelling to understand how individual behaviour contributes to population-level social structure.\n\n## Research Interests\n\n- Social evolution\n\n- Cooperative behaviour\n\n- Nest fidelity\n\n- Dispersal and philopatry\n\n- Social networks\n\n- Behavioural ecology of bees\n\n## Current Research Themes\n\n### Social Organization in Carpenter Bees\n\nUnderstanding how reproductive behaviour, nest use, and social interactions contribute to the formation and maintenance of social groups.\n\n### Sleeping Associations\n\nInvestigating sex-specific patterns of sleeping associations and partner fidelity.\n\n### Nest Fidelity and Dispersal\n\nExamining how individuals move among nests and the implications for social evolution.\n\n### Environmental Variation\n\nUnderstanding how weather and resource availability influence maternal investment and offspring production.\n\n## Quick Links\n\n- [Research](https://m365.cloud.microsoft/chat/conversation/research.qmd)\n\n- [Publications](https://m365.cloud.microsoft/chat/conversation/publications.qmd)\n\n- [Teaching](https://m365.cloud.microsoft/chat/conversation/teaching.qmd)\n\n- [CV](https://m365.cloud.microsoft/chat/conversation/cv.qmd)\n\n- [Contact](https://m365.cloud.microsoft/chat/conversation/contact.qmd)\n","srcMarkdownNoYaml":""},"formats":{"html":{"identifier":{"display-name":"HTML","target-format":"html","base-format":"html"},"execute":{"fig-width":7,"fig-height":5,"fig-format":"retina","fig-dpi":96,"df-print":"default